.\" Automatically generated by Pandoc 3.2
.\"
.TH "rofi\-actions" "5" "" "rofi" "File Formats Manual"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
\f[B]rofi\-actions\f[R] \- Custom commands following interaction with
rofi menus
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
\f[B]rofi\f[R] allows to set custom commands or scripts to be executed
when some actions are performed in the menu, such as changing selection,
accepting an entry or canceling.
.PP
This makes it possible for example to play sound effects or read aloud
menu entries on selection.
.SH "نحوه استفاده (USAGE)"
Following is the list of rofi flags for specifying custom commands or
scripts to execute on supported actions:
.TP
\f[B]\-on\-selection\-changed\f[R] \f[I]cmd\f[R]
Command or script to run when the current selection changes.
Selected text is forwarded to the command replacing the pattern
\f[I]{entry}\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-on\-entry\-accepted\f[R] \f[I]cmd\f[R]
Command or script to run when a menu entry is accepted.
Accepted text is forwarded to the command replacing the pattern
\f[I]{entry}\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-on\-mode\-changed\f[R] \f[I]cmd\f[R]
Command or script to run when the menu mode (e.g.\ drun,window,ssh\&...)
is changed.
.TP
\f[B]\-on\-menu\-canceled\f[R] \f[I]cmd\f[R]
Command or script to run when the menu is canceled.
.TP
\f[B]\-on\-menu\-error\f[R] \f[I]cmd\f[R]
Command or script to run when an error menu is shown (e.g.\ \f[B]rofi
\-e \[dq]error message\[dq]\f[R]).
Error text is forwarded to the command replacing the pattern
\f[I]{error}\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-on\-screenshot\-taken\f[R] \f[I]cmd\f[R]
Command or script to run when a screenshot of rofi is taken.
Screenshot path is forwarded to the command replacing the pattern
\f[I]{path}\f[R].
.SS Example usage
Rofi command line:
.IP
.EX
rofi \-on\-selection\-changed \[dq]/path/to/select.sh {entry}\[dq] \[rs]
     \-on\-entry\-accepted \[dq]/path/to/accept.sh {entry}\[dq] \[rs]
     \-on\-menu\-canceled \[dq]/path/to/exit.sh\[dq] \[rs]
     \-on\-mode\-changed \[dq]/path/to/change.sh\[dq] \[rs]
     \-on\-menu\-error \[dq]/path/to/error.sh {error}\[dq] \[rs]
     \-on\-screenshot\-taken \[dq]/path/to/camera.sh {path}\[dq] \[rs]
     \-show drun
.EE
.PP
Rofi config file:
.IP
.EX
configuration {
    on\-selection\-changed: \[dq]/path/to/select.sh {entry}\[dq];
    on\-entry\-accepted: \[dq]/path/to/accept.sh {entry}\[dq];
    on\-menu\-canceled: \[dq]/path/to/exit.sh\[dq];
    on\-mode\-changed: \[dq]/path/to/change.sh\[dq];
    on\-menu\-error: \[dq]/path/to/error.sh {error}\[dq];
    on\-screenshot\-taken: \[dq]/path/to/camera.sh {path}\[dq];
}
.EE
.SS Play sound effects
Here\[cq]s an example bash script that plays a sound effect using
\f[B]aplay\f[R] when the current selection is changed:
.IP
.EX
\f[I]#!/bin/bash\f[R]

coproc aplay \-q $HOME/Music/selecting_an_item.wav
.EE
.PP
The use of \f[B]coproc\f[R] for playing sounds is suggested, otherwise
the rofi process will wait for sounds to end playback before exiting.
.SS Read aloud
Here\[cq]s an example bash script that reads aloud currently selected
entries using \f[B]espeak\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
\f[I]#!/bin/bash\f[R]

killall espeak
echo \[dq]selected: $\[at]\[dq] \f[B]|\f[R] espeak
.EE
